{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat AGENTS.md && rg -n 'F3|3\\\\.5|3\\\\.7|C1|AX150|compact|reference' docs/02-product-spec.md docs/03-plan-typescript-release.md reviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/docs.review.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat AGENTS.md && rg -n 'F3|3\\\\.5|3\\\\.7|C1|AX150|compact|reference' docs/02-product-spec.md docs/03-plan-typescript-release.md reviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/docs.review.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Working in this repository\n\nAxylo is a browser charting library. The product is specified in `docs/02-product-spec.md`; the build plan is `docs/03-plan-typescript-release.md`. Read the sections your task names before writing code.\n\n## Rules for every change\n\n- **Contracts are fixed.** `packages/axylo/src/core/contracts.ts` and `packages/axylo/src/public.ts` are the interfaces between modules. Do not edit them. If your work needs a change there, stop that part, finish what you can, and describe the exact change you need in your report.\n- **Stay in your files.** Each task lists the directories it owns. Do not create, edit or delete anything else, including configuration and other modules. Several agents work in this checkout at the same time.\n- **No runtime dependencies.** Use the platform (`Intl`, typed arrays). Dev dependencies already installed: TypeScript, Vitest, fast-check, esbuild, Playwright (system Chrome), axe-core. The network is not available; do not try to install anything.\n- **No DOM at import time.** A module that needs the DOM takes it as a parameter or touches it inside a function. Pure stages (data, scales, formatting, layout, scene) must run in Node.\n- **Hot paths use typed arrays.** No object per data point, no array of arrays per data point, no copying of large columns that the contracts say are borrowed.\n- **Never guess silently.** Anything that cannot be drawn as given is reported through the `DiagnosticSink` with the code from spec section 3.5.\n- **Tests come from the spec.** Expected values are derived from the specification and the fixture data, never by running the implementation and pasting its output. Use fast-check property tests for invariants (\"for any data …\"). A test you cannot make pass is reported as failing; do not weaken it or change its expected value.\n- **TypeScript strict, no `any`** in exported signatures. `__DEV__` is a build-time boolean (true in tests).\n- **Comments say why**, not what. Names are plain words.\n- **Do not commit.** The coordinator commits.\n\n## Commands\n\n```bash\nnpm run typecheck      # tsc over the library, its tests, and the API examples in docs/api\nnpm test               # unit and property tests (Node)\nnpm run build          # packages/axylo/dist\nnpm run test:browser   # browser tests against the built bundle, in system Chrome\n```\n\n## Your report\n\nEnd with a short report: what you built (files), what you verified and how (paste the last lines of the test run), what is not done or not verified, any contract change you need, and any place where the spec was ambiguous and what you assumed. Keep \"ran and saw\" apart from \"expect\".\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/docs.review.md:27:6. **B · The three headline KPIs disagree with the data plotted beneath them.** `examples/compact-tiles.html:10–21,29–35`, embedded at `pages/compact.md:9`. **Ran** the fixture arithmetic. The 30-day totals are **50,781 sessions** and **$184,909**, while the cards say 48,210 and $182,400. The latest daily error count and the 30-day daily mean are both 30, while the card says 37. Derive the headlines from `rows` and label the error statistic explicitly, for example “Errors on the latest day.” [Example](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/apps/docs/examples/compact-tiles.html:10)\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/docs.review.md:37:11. **B · An invisible compact reference can flatten the entire sparkline.** `pages/compact.md:23–27`, `options.md:81–83`, `line.md:43`, `bar.md:46`, `scatter.md:41`. **Ran** a compact line with values 2–4 and a reference at 1,000. Its y domain became `[0,1000]`, and the reference entered the summary. Replace “have no effect” with “compact charts hide reference marks, but references still affect automatic domains and the description.” On full charts, author bounds can exclude a reference. A horizontal bar chart also swaps the screen directions of x and y references. [Domain calculation](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/view/index.ts:258) · [Reader description](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/reader/index.ts:221)\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/docs.review.md:41:13. **B · The documented x-kind vote predicts the wrong axis.** `pages/data.md:75–83`, `data/diagnostics.mjs:114–117` (AX107). **Ran** three categorical strings, two dates and two numbers. “Takes the kind most of them have” predicts category. The chart selected date, retained the two dates and reported AX107. Category wins if its count is at least the **combined** recognized count. Otherwise the largest recognized kind wins, with a fixed tie order. Recommend an explicit x type for heterogeneous feeds. AX107 also covers unusable numeric x, series or donut labels, and invalid domains or references, where the option can be ignored without dropping a data row. [Vote](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/data/x.ts:122) · [Reference validation](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/view/references.ts:24)\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/docs.review.md:43:14. **B · The diagnostic severity is insufficient to predict what remains on screen or whether a call throws.** `pages/options.md:20`, `diagnostics.md:25–29,53`, `data.md:127`, `line.md:42`, `scatter.md:23`, `data/diagnostics.mjs:128–132,368–372,428–433`, `lib/site.mjs:413–416` (AX108, AX150, AX199). **Ran** the series and scatter cases. Duplicate x can suppress one series while peers still draw. With no drawable series the chart shows an error state and retains an inspectable table where available. A scatter y **list** can produce warning AX150 and an error state. The generic “option is ignored” outcome is wrong there. **Reasoned** from strict delivery that a presentation-stage AX199 does not throw from the original call. Its underlying exception can go to `console.error`, while the diagnostic follows diagnostic delivery. Generate severity text separately from the specific effect and phase. [Error-state selection](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:924) · [Delivery](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/delivery.ts:65)\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/docs.review.md:45:15. **B · The chart-type “Limit” rows conflate rows, marks and available visual distinctions.** `pages/scatter.md:7,38–40`, `line.md:41`, `area.md:40`, `bar.md:44–45`, `compact.md:21`, `index.md:18`, `data/diagnostics.mjs:230–233,246–249,261–264,277–280` (AX130–133). **Ran** scatter with valid x and unplottable y. It had no point but did have an in-range table row reading **No data**. AX133 concerns more than 50,000 plottable points. The view draws visible points without simplification. **Reasoned** from the cue and geometry code that eight is a warning threshold. Bars use fill patterns, including in multiseries compact mode, with 32 distinct default combinations before repetition. AX132 compares visible x slots with CSS pixels. It does not establish that every grouped bar is thinner than one pixel. [Scatter normalization](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/data/normalize.ts:348) · [Table](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/reader/table.ts:121) · [Bar widths and patterns](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/scene/bars.ts:74) · [Spec F9](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/docs/02-product-spec.md:102)\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/docs.review.md:49:17. **B · The accessibility claims exceed the evidence allowed by §3.8.** `pages/index.md:3`, `compact.md:3`, `accessibility.md:3,11–17,54–64`, `updating.md:49`, `migrate-chartjs.md:33,64`. **Reasoned** from the evidence record and focused-text implementation. Replace “works with … a screen reader”, “can rely on”, and unconditional claims about what is spoken with observable behavior. The chart exposes a name, summary, focused value text and polite state updates. Appending alone need not rewrite a focused value just because its ordinal changed, but a changed or evicted focused datum can update it. Speech depends on the reader. State the limits alongside the claims: automated structure checks, developer rehearsal planned, no screen reader run in the cited evidence, no usability testing with disabled users, and Firefox, Safari and phones unverified. The recorded browser evidence is desktop Chrome. [Spec §3.8](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/docs/02-product-spec.md:214) · [Focused-text decision](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/docs/decisions/0004-tooltip-and-focused-text.md)\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/docs.review.md:55:20. **M · Link and include checks can approve material that will be missing or wrong on the published site.** `lib/site.mjs:239–247,251–264,274–293,458–483`, `lib/markdown.mjs:131–148`. **Ran** the checker on the existing output. It returned zero broken links, although the 19 top-level HTML pages contained **58 references to 55 distinct `../…` destinations**. The checker can satisfy these from the checkout. **Reasoned** that serving `dist/` alone loses source files and decision records or resolves them to different resources. Publish the linked files or use revision-pinned repository links, then check against the deployment root. Validate `[table: …]` targets, which are currently ignored. Restrict source includes to intended canonical paths and fail on missing required snippets. Two adjacent directive lines also become one ordinary paragraph unless separated by a blank line. Treat each directive as a block. [Include implementation](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/apps/docs/lib/site.mjs:244) · [Link checker](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/apps/docs/lib/site.mjs:458)\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/docs.review.md:76:   | AX102 `:41`, AX103 `:55` | An absent y can become zero under the declared policy. An absent x or series can drop a row. Non-finite domain/reference inputs can cause an option to be ignored. `NaN` in a floating typed value column is ordinary missing data. |\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/docs.review.md:91:   | Recharts and React versions, wide fixture, one `Line` per key, supplied colours, tick formatter, omitted reference line, mount helper and new-array stream | **Harness and installed manifests.** The harness shows what this example supplies. It cannot establish minimality, that Recharts requires this row shape, or the official provenance of the example colours. The missing long label is a historical observation at the comparison width. [Recharts harness](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/research/harness/src/libs/recharts.jsx) · [Mount helper](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/research/harness/src/libs/_react.jsx) |\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/docs.review.md:94:28. **M · The options reference omits information needed to use formatting, domains and localization correctly.** `pages/data.md:7,136`, `options.md:29,62,81,114,139–141,227`, `accessibility.md:50`, `stability.md:34`. **Ran** the default tick formatter at 50,000 and got `50,000`, where the page gives `50K`. Compact defaults begin at a largest tick of one million, with scientific notation for extreme scales. **Reasoned** from the public types that `XValue` should be defined on first use as `number | string | Date`, and `{ columns }` should say one equal-length `ArrayLike` per field. In a wide chart the first y field supplies the shared domain. Replace “Every built-in string” with “reader-facing messages”. Developer diagnostics have fixed registry wording. Give a translated note retaining `{seeTable}`, which the reader can remove with the table disabled. The generated defaults pick up `panLeft`, `panRight`, `jumpNotFound`, `plotInstructions`, `seeTable`, `totalMixed`, `incompleteAt` and `incompleteCount` on a successful rebuild. Also change “Take seven numbers” to “four days, two readings per day.” [Tick formatting](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/format/number.ts:200) · [Shared domain](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/stages.ts:91) · [Conditional table text](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/reader/index.ts:49)\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/docs.review.md:116:| `compact-tiles`, `compact-dirty` | Pass both | The dirty-data example supplies its own tile and demonstrates the disclosure. The three-card example’s headlines disagree with its source rows. |\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/docs.review.md:117:| `a11y-card`, `states`, `units` | Pass all three | Show author-supplied naming/context, four state panels, and ratio/unit formatting. `units` explicitly requests compact ticks in one panel, so it cannot establish the claimed default. |\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/docs.review.md:148:compact.md             4  (#6, #11, #15, #17)\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/docs.review.md:188:AX150                  1  (#14)\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:3:Revision 3, 2026-11-18. Revised after three independent reviews ([ledger](../reviews/2026-11-18/ledger.md)) and the owner's decisions of the same day (scatter and a compact variant are in 1.0; the mark renderer is decided in M1).\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:71:  y: { field: 'sessions', label: 'Sessions', unit: 'sessions', tickFormat: { notation: 'compact' } },\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:92:Summarized; the declarations are the reference.\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:99:| `zoom`, `reference` | Cartesian charts only. |\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:100:| `compact` | Line, area and bar: marks only, as a static image with a text alternative (spec 3.7). |\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:103:| `strict`, `onDiagnostic` | Diagnostics delivery (section 3.5 of the spec). |\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:105:There is no `width`, `height`, `responsive`, `theme`, `palette` or `animation` option. Size comes from the container, colors from CSS, motion from the spec (I5). An unknown key raises AX150 with the closest known name.\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:132:The registry, with each code's level and outcome, is in the spec (section 3.5). Example for the Phase 1 combined dirty fixture (`[10, 20, null, NaN, '40', undefined, 70]`):\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:264:- The benchmark harness from the performance plan, section 3: readiness markers, main-thread accounting, the reference-machine record, and adapters for uPlot and Chart.js. It measures those two before any Axylo code exists.\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:286:- The diagnostic registry (F3, F12); missing values and absent steps (F2); the three temporal types (F4); formatting (F6); domains (F7); sorting and duplicates (F11); `validate()`.\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:294:Example: \"What Axylo tells you about your data\". Docs: Diagnostics reference, one page per code; Dates and time zones.\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:298:- Title, `labelledBy`, subtitle, axis titles; toolbar with legend toggles; full tooltip and fixed readout (I1); label fitting (L1) and the too-small fallback (L8); states (L7); reference lines and bands.\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:322:### M5. Bar, area, donut, scatter and the compact variant (ceiling: 18 days)\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:324:Each type is done when its column of the type matrix (spec 3.6) and every applicable row of the acceptance matrix pass, including the accessibility and performance rows. Types are finished one at a time, in this order: bar, area, donut, the compact variant, scatter.\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:331:- Compact variant: criteria C1–C5; a page of 40 adds no tab stops and meets P8.\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:405:| Annotations beyond reference lines and bands | Text placement interacts with L1. |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:3:Revision 3, 2026-11-18. Revised after three independent reviews ([ledger](../reviews/2026-11-18/ledger.md)), then updated with the owner's decisions of the same day: scatter is in 1.0, a compact variant is in 1.0, and the mark renderer is decided by measurement in M1.\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:25:| uPlot | The speed reference | Automatic sizing, a palette, bars and donuts without path builders, and an accessibility layer, at a speed the budgets in section 5 keep honest |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:59:Plus, on every cartesian chart: reference lines and bands (a target, an incident window).\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:61:The Phase 1 harness exercised line, bar and donut in all ten libraries (donut in nine; uPlot has none). Area and scatter are added on judgment; Phase 1 found no usage data by chart type. Two reviewers argued for fewer types and one for a compact variant; the owner decided on all five types plus the compact variant. Scatter alone needs two-dimensional hit testing and its own navigation model, so it is built last and carries the most schedule risk.\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:96:| F3 | Input that cannot be plotted as given is reported, never guessed. The diagnostic registry (section 3.5) fixes each case's level, what is drawn and what the reader sees. | One test per code; the combined `dirty` fixture and the four one-bad-value fixtures yield exactly the codes listed in section 3.5 | R5, D5 |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:99:| F6 | Numbers and dates are formatted for the page locale. Ticks and readouts are formatted separately: ticks may be compact (`50K`); tooltip, table and announcements show the full integer part, and the fraction with up to six significant digits not counting the fraction's leading zeros (`123,456.75`; `0.000123456`; `0.1 + 0.2` reads `0.3`), with the unit. A custom formatter that throws falls back to the default and raises a diagnostic. | Expected strings for chosen values (large integers, small decimals, percentages, zoned times) in `en-US`, `de-DE` and `en-IN` | R4 |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:100:| F7 | Domains follow one order of precedence: the zoomed view is inside the author's `domain` if given, otherwise inside the automatic domain. The automatic domain contains all data, reference lines and stack totals, and ends at the first tick at or beyond each extreme. A field declared `scale: 'percent'` (0–100) or `'ratio'` (0–1) ends at full scale only when its maximum is at least half of full scale and not above it. Nothing is inferred from a label. | Property tests; `bars` ends at 100 when declared `percent`; a 4% maximum ends at the first tick at or above 4% | R1 |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:114:| L4 | Light or dark is taken from the chart element's computed `color-scheme`; if that is not set, from the luminance of the inherited text color. `--axylo-background` overrides both. Marks repaint within one frame when the scheme, forced colors, contrast preference, or the `class`, `style` or `data-theme` of `<html>` or `<body>` changes. Forced-colors mode uses system colors. | A page that sets `color-scheme`; a class-toggled dark theme without it; a light-only page on a dark device (must stay light); a runtime toggle; forced-colors emulation | R10 |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:116:| L6 | Title, subtitle and axis titles with units are part of the chart. A value axis is titled with its label (the field name when none is given) and unit. An x axis that is a measure (number) is titled the same way; a time, date or category x axis is titled only when the author gives a `label`, since its ticks already say what it is. A reference line or band shows its label next to it. Axis titles never overlap tick labels. | Layout tests; `trend` fixture | R9 |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:148:### 3.5 Diagnostic registry\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:174:| AX150 | Warning | Unknown option key | Ignored; the message suggests the closest known key |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:176:| AX131 | Hint | A compact chart has more than one series | Drawn, with dash differences |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:200:### 3.7 Compact variant\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:202:`compact: true` on line, area and bar draws the marks and nothing else: no axes, gridlines, legend, toolbar, table control, zoom or tooltip. It is for a small tile where the page already shows the number and the label.\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:206:| C1 | A compact chart is a static image with a full text alternative: `role=\"img\"`, an accessible name (as in A1, including AX140 when none is given) and the generated summary as its description (series, x range, minimum, maximum, last value, omissions). It has no tab stop and no pointer-only behavior, so nothing is available to a mouse that is not available to a keyboard. | Accessibility-tree snapshot; a page of 40 has zero added tab stops |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:207:| C2 | The fidelity rules still hold: zero baseline for bar and area (F1), gaps (F2), diagnostics (F3), simplified drawing (F5), sorting (F11), no motion (I5), scheme from the page (L4). | The same fixtures as the full charts |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:209:| C4 | With more than one series, lines differ by dash as well as color, since there is no legend; AX131 suggests one series per compact chart. | Two-series fixture |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:210:| C5 | When values were left out (F12), the description says so and a small marker with a text equivalent appears in the corner. | `dirty` fixture in compact mode |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:212:A compact chart does not give access to every value; the summary is its alternative. An author who needs every value reachable uses the full chart.\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:224:| DX3 | With typed rows, a misspelled field, a text field on a value axis, wide `y` combined with `series`, and an option that does not apply to the chart type all fail to compile. At run time, for untyped rows, the same mistakes raise AX101, AX106 and AX150. | [docs/api/examples.ts](api/examples.ts) compiles and each marked mistake fails (already checked with TypeScript 7.0.2); runtime tests per code | D5 |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:225:| DX4 | Diagnostics follow the registry in section 3.5: stable code, chart name, field and rows where they apply, the fix, and a documentation page per code. | Message snapshots; link checker | R5, D5 |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:239:| ID | Workload | Metric | Statistic | Provisional limit | Phase 1 reference |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:241:| P1 | `trend` (3×120), default options, reference desktop | Main-thread task time from the call until the chart is complete | Median of 20 runs | 10 ms | Not comparable across libraries below about 35 ms with the Phase 1 method |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:247:| P8 | 40 compact charts created on one page, each 160 × 48 px with one series | Total main-thread task time | Median of 20 | 80 ms | Not measured in Phase 1 |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:262:| Diagnostics are a first-class feature with codes | R5: none of the ten named the field, the row or the problem. | Kept. Severity and delivery rewritten (3.5): readers are told too, and production builds are not silent. |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:270:| Canvas marks with DOM text | D9: a canvas library is the speed reference. D10: one DOM node per point is slow. | **Reopened.** Phase 1 does not show that SVG is slow, only that one node per point is; a single SVG path per series was fast. M1 builds both mark renderers on the same scene and measures them (section 8). Canvas is the working assumption. |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:275:| Chart types | Judgment, then the owner's decision. | All five in 1.0, plus the compact variant (3.7). |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:292:Settled by the owner on 2026-11-18: scatter is in 1.0; the compact variant is in 1.0; the mark renderer stays open until M1 measures both.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
